Creators and validator for the split layout. Mirrors the Cyberdeck
aiu-context-add pattern: creation writes a correctly-shaped file (loud
on collision), discovery is free (recursive loader in mm order),
tracking is an explicit validator (not memory). No manifest, no
registry edit — dropping a tagged file is the whole registration.

A new state needs three things (the creator does #1, you do #2–3):
1. =states/<name>= (creator writes it),
2. a =biomechanical-input-interface-define-state= invocation in
   =engine/state-machine.org=,
3. =init-state-fn= routing in =engine/setup.org= if the state should
   activate automatically.
A new leader needs only its file (the main =SPC= hub links sub-hydras
by body symbol at runtime).

